<div id="q-persistent-identifier" class="question">
    <h3>13. How will the application of a unique and persistent identifier (such as a Digital Object Identifier (DOI)) to each data set be ensured?</h3>

    <div class="answer">
    {# Metadata specification #}
    {%- if data.dmp.sharedResources.metadataSpecifications |length > 0 -%}
        {%- set n = data.dmp.sharedResources.metadataSpecifications | length -%}
        {%- if n > 1 -%}
            <p>In our {{ globals.projects }}, there are {{ data.dmp.sharedResources.metadataSpecifications | length }} approaches towards persistent identifiers assignment.</p>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if n > 1 -%}<ul>{%- endif -%}
        {%- for metadata in data.dmp.sharedResources.metadataSpecifications -%}
            {%- if n > 1 -%}<li style="margin-bottom: 2em;">{%- else -%}<div style="margin-bottom: 2em;">{%- endif -%}

            {{ macros.datasetIntro(metadata, "persistent identifiers assignment", data.dmp.datasets) }}

            {%- if metadata.usesPids._value is sameas true -%}
                {%- if metadata.whoProvidesPids._value -%}
                    <p>
                    {%- if metadata.whoProvidesPids._value == "project" -%}
                        A persistent identifier (PID) for this data will be assigned by the project’s data steward or principal investigator.
                    {%- elif metadata.whoProvidesPids._value == "institutional" -%}
                        A persistent identifier (PID) for this data will be assigned by the institutional data steward.
                    {%- elif metadata.whoProvidesPids._value == "repository" -%}
                        A persistent identifier (PID) for this data will be assigned automatically by the data repository upon submission.
                    {%- elif metadata.whoProvidesPids._value == "provider" -%}
                        A persistent identifier (PID) for this data will be assigned by the national or international PID service provider.
                    {%- else -%}
                        A persistent identifier (PID) for this data will be assigned by {{ metadata.whoProvidesPids._value }}.
                    {%- endif -%}
                    {{ macros.linkQuestion(metadata.whoProvidesPids._path) }}
                    </p>
                {%- endif -%}
            {%- elif metadata.usesPids._value is sameas false -%}
                <p>A persistent identifier (PID) for this data will not be assigned.{{ macros.linkQuestion(metadata.usesPids._path) }}</p>
            {%- else -%}
                <p>It is not specified whether a persistent identifier (PID) will be assigned for this data.</p>
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- if n > 1 -%}</li>{%- else -%}</div>{%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
        {%- if n > 1 -%}</ul>{%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {# Generated Datasets #}
    <h4>Generated Datasets</h4>
    {%- if data.dmp.datasets|length > 0 -%}
        The following dataset{{ "s" if data.dmp.datasets|length > 1 }} will be generated in this {{globals.projects}}, for which persistent identifiers (PIDs) will be assigned:
        <ul>
        {%- for dataset in data.dmp.datasets -%}
            <li>
            {%- if dataset.name -%}
                <strong>{{ dataset.name._value }}</strong>{{ macros.linkQuestion(dataset.name._path) }}
            {%- else -%}
                <strong>(no name given)</strong>
            {%- endif -%}

            {# Identifier #}
            {%- if dataset.identifiers|length > 0 %}
                <ul>
                {%- for identifier in dataset.identifiers -%}
                    <li>
                    {{ macros.formatIdentifier(identifier) }}
                    </li>
                {%- endfor -%}
                </ul>
            {%- else %}
                <em>(No persistent identifier (PID) has been assigned)</em>
            {%- endif %}
            </li>
        {%- endfor -%}
        </ul>
    {%- else -%}
        <p>No datasets will be generated in this {{ globals.projects }}; therefore, no persistent identifiers (PIDs) are defined.</p>
    {%- endif -%}

    <p>Details on which PID systems are used in different repositories are provided in Section 4, Question 10.</p>
    </div>
</div>
